Call Log Merger Using a Linked List — Complete Project Guide
A Call Log Merger using a Linked List is a data structures project that combines call records from two or more call logs into one unified call log. It can store, display, search, sort, and merge call records using a linked list.

This project is useful for learning Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA), especially linked lists, insertion, traversal, searching, sorting, and merging.

1. What is a Call Log Merger?
A call log is a collection of records containing details about phone calls, such as:

Caller name

Phone number

Call date and time

Call duration

Call type (incoming, outgoing, or missed)

A call log merger combines records from different lists into one list. Depending on the requirements, it can also remove duplicate calls and arrange records chronologically.

